<title>UK: UK grain traders bid for wheat and barley refunds.</title>
<headline>UK grain traders bid for wheat and barley refunds.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK grain traders bid for a total of 16,100 tonnes of free market wheat and 88,000 tonnes of free market barley export refunds at Thursday's weekly European Union (EU) grain tender, the UK Intervention Board of Agricultural Produce said.</p>
<p>Wheat refund bids ranged from 12.99 to 20.48 Ecu's a tonne and barley from 30.99 to 37 Ecu's, the board added.</p>
<p>All bids will be considered at Thursday's weekly EU cereals management committee meeting.</p>
<p>--Jim Ballantyne, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8062</p>
</text>
